  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason includes the aspiration level (1750), the positive differences (2250 for 4000, 1250 for 3000), and the probabilities of positive differences (20% for B, 25% for A). The individual did not mention any reference to an aspiration level or differences from a mean. However, their justification—choosing the lottery with the higher probability of a non-zero outcome (3000 vs. 4000)—aligns with the decision reason's rule, which also prefers the lottery with higher probability of positive deviation from the aspiration level. Although the individual did not explicitly use the aspiration level or calculate deviations, the core logic of preferring higher probability of a favorable outcome (i.e., positive difference from a benchmark) matches the reason’s rule. The individual’s focus on probability over value is consistent with the reason’s emphasis on the likelihood of positive differences. Thus, while the process is not identical, the underlying criterion is aligned. It is plausible that the individual implicitly used a similar mental benchmark, even if not stated. Therefore, the reason was likely used, though not explicitly described.",
  "final_assessment_score": 75
}

{
